Boot diagnostics for the usermanagerd/persona wall (all default-off).

Four boot-args; no behaviour change unless one is set:

  sweetexeclog=0          suppress the per-exec "exec NAME" console line (the
                          exec flood hides launchd's boot-task lines)
  sweetexecwatch=a,b,c    "EXECW NAME pid N" when a listed process is exec'd
                          and "EXITW NAME pid N status X" when it exits
                          (exit1() in bsd/kern/kern_exit.c)
  sweetrenameswap=1       one "SWEET RENAMESWAP: proc flags err from X to Y"
                          line per RENAME_SWAP attempt, printed at the
                          renameat_internal() exit path where the final error
                          is known; this also covers the swap-with-missing-
                          target ENOENT that returns before vn_rename()
  sweetfsprobe=1          at 120/240/480 s of uptime stat these paths from the
                          kernel and print one line each:
                          "FSPROBE <path> err=<e> size=<n> mode=<o> fileid=<i>"
                          /private/var/keybags/{systembag,persona,usersession}.kb
                          /private/var/mobile/Containers, /private/var/containers,
                          /private/var/folders, /private/var/containers/Data/System

Live evidence this addresses: usermanagerd's boot task completes (UMD_INIT /
EARLYBOOT SETUP DONE) without a visible write error, but /private/var/keybags
still contains only systembag.kb.  EXECW/EXITW shows whether usermanagerd
really exits and with which status, sweetrenameswap shows whether Foundation's
atomic swap rename (0052) is attempted and whether it succeeds, and
sweetfsprobe shows the on-disk result (a later boot then reports persona.kb's
size and mode).

Base: bsd/kern/kern_exec.c, bsd/kern/kern_exit.c, bsd/vfs/vfs_syscalls.c and
bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c from xnuios/xnu-src/xnu with 0001..0125 applied.
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
